THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT UNDER A SINGLE LICENCE. Which terms apply depends on
which directory a file is in, and the split is deliberate — it is the
frontier between the parts of the product that are proprietary and the part
that must be free software.

  blender/    GNU General Public License v3 or later.  See blender/LICENSE.
              Anything that imports `bpy` and is published has to be
              GPL-compatible, because Blender's Python API is part of
              Blender and Blender is GPL.

  core/       Proprietary, all rights reserved.  See core/LICENSE.
  firmware/   Proprietary, all rights reserved.  See firmware/LICENSE.
              Neither imports `bpy`. The core is an independent program
              that runs, and is useful, with no Blender on the machine, and
              speaks to consumers over a documented network protocol. The
              firmware is not PC software at all: it is burned onto a
              microcontroller.

  everything  Proprietary, all rights reserved, under the terms in
  else        core/LICENSE, unless a LICENSE file in a nearer directory
              says otherwise. This includes docs/, scripts/, samples/ and
              tests/.

The rule that keeps this coherent: the extension package uploaded to the
Blender extensions platform contains ONLY the contents of blender/. The
core is never distributed inside it — the extension consumes the core over
the network and does not bundle it.

Publication of this source is not a grant of any licence to it. See each
LICENSE file for the terms that do apply.
